 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "night_day, growth (life from the dead as a parable) and wheat for Allah's signs; no motif on the negated alliance (28:1-8) or on «نفسه». 29: As-Sa'di's entry repeats verse 28, so 29 uses Al-Muyassar. 28:17-21 uses As-Sa'di's shared core of the exception (fearing for one's life); the tafsirs differ on what more it allows. STAGING v4: 27: fields at dusk (night entering day) with a farmer; crops sprout on «وتخرج الحي من الميت» (both tafsirs: the crop from the seed); no withering is drawn for the opposite (the tafsirs give seeds and eggs, not death); the farmer catches a sparkle on «وترزق». Plates night_day, growth, wheat as before. 28-29: believers and disbelievers in a town; the believers turn away from them on «أولياء» (keeping the prohibition); no gesture on the conditional «ومن يفعل», the disputed exception «إلا أن تتقوا» or the conditional «إن تخفوا». Allah's knowledge only as a light plate and the stars plate (ended before the Name). Cover moved to the believers' chapter to match its title."
 },
